EcoLoom System Walkthrough & Verification Report🌟 Executive SummaryEcoLoom is an end-to-end AI-powered geospatial platform designed for environmental restoration authorities, forestry departments, and ESG carbon developers. It monitors afforestation density across any user-selected Region of Interest (ROI) using simulated Sentinel-2 multi-spectral satellite imagery, calculates high-resolution NDVI vegetation indices, automatically discovers allocatable public barren plots (excluding water bodies and private/built-up properties via spatial masking), and applies a multi-criteria scoring algorithm to recommend native plant species tailored to local micro-environmental conditions.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🛰️ 1. Core Architecture & Workflowflowchart TD
    A[User Selects ROI or Preset Hotspot] --> B[Satellite Engine: Spectral Reflectance & NDVI]
    B --> C[Spatial Masking: OSM Exclusions & Parcel Bank]
    C --> D[Micro-Environmental & Agronomic Profiling]
    D --> E[ML Ensemble Model: 4-Pillar ExtraTreesRegressor]
    E --> F[Interactive Map Canvas & Telemetry Inspection]
    F --> G[Dossier & GeoJSON Export]

